      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T14:08:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know the chromium style guide doesn\u0027t apply to dawn but there was a [detailed discussion](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/cxx/c/bBY0gZa1Otk) about using std::byte for it. I think the TLDR is std::byte is badly named and not appropriate for use with binary data. That lead to it being banned in chromium in favour of using uint8_t for byte data.\n\nI need to reread the discuss but I think it applies here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "8ea7ed5f7b44d8263ded7232ece952b670d84627",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
