        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T18:14:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I reread the thread and I guess BlobCache is kind of the place where std::byte is sort of reasonable. BlobCache treats it as opaque bytes and does do much of anything with the data other than copying it. Using span\u003cuint8_t\u003e feels more easier to me but that also what I\u0027m used to so I\u0027ll leave that up to Dawn folks to decide.\n\nI left a couple suggestions on the first part of the CL but I\u0027ll hold off looking at the rest until byte vs uint8_t is settled.",
      "parentUuid": "a09a1491_46bdf069",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "8ea7ed5f7b44d8263ded7232ece952b670d84627",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bf4da2c_76f80c1f",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Blob.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T20:53:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve addressed other comments minus the byte vs uint8_t, and factored some code into preceding CLs. The reason I chose to use byte in this change was because in Kai\u0027s doc: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-4tHoIIIdefvRxw0wT5PVSV9_Sec2eOURIYSXi0DGFU/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-Lm-fWYMRv-oscgEzHnvpEw\u0026tab\u003dt.0 using std::byte was something he called out. Honestly, I don\u0027t really feel particular to either directions, so I added Kai to this change as a reviewer also to see if he has any preferences on top of Brandon\u0027s.",
      "parentUuid": "d1b09887_edac662d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "8ea7ed5f7b44d8263ded7232ece952b670d84627",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af57f4e2_af387731",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Blob.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T19:35:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel the same way as Kyle, it seems like there\u0027s no very clear criteria for what we should do. But I lean toward using std::byte in Dawn for the following reasons:\n- Unlike Chromium, it is practical for us to change ALL usages of char/uint8_t/void* to std::byte (I already started looking at it a few weeks ago and I think it will be fairly easy)\n- Unlike Chromium, we intend for Dawn to work with strict aliasing enabled (AFAIK)\n\nAnd I think the guideline should be that we use it for any data that will be reinterpreted.\n\nAs for using it in this interface specifically, this will force std::byte to be used in Chromium, right? Will it require us to bypass the std::byte ban for a nontrivial amount of Chromium code? If yes, maybe we should use uint8_t here just for practicality.",
      "parentUuid": "1bf4da2c_76f80c1f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "8ea7ed5f7b44d8263ded7232ece952b670d84627",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70d8c653_102b3277",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Blob.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 46,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T19:42:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As for using it in this interface specifically, this will force std::byte to be used in Chromium, right?\n\nRight now webgpu_cpp.h defines DefineCachingInterface in terms of C types defines in webgpu.h so WGPUDawnLoadCacheDataFunction uses void*+size_t. Unless that changes there is zero impact on Chromium since this is all internal implementation details.\n\nIf webgpu_cpp.h was able to define caching functions using modern C++ types, eg. std::span\u003cstd::byte\u003e instead of void*+size_t, in the future then I still don\u0027t think it matters to Chrome. The std::span\u003cstd::byte\u003e can be converted to a base::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e at the interface boundary. Since Chrome doesn\u0027t use std::span it requires conversion regardless.",
      "parentUuid": "af57f4e2_af387731",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 46,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 46,
        "endChar": 42
      },
